WEBVTT

00:29.901 --> 00:32.411
Lifeforce Transfer has ended!

00:43.771 --> 00:48.051
Is it true that Elymas 
is living it up in Rondalm?

00:51.881 --> 00:54.101
I'm not certain,

00:54.101 --> 00:58.601
but I've heard someone very similar to him 
has achieved exceptional success there.

01:03.011 --> 01:05.861
You don't waste time. Bring it on!

01:07.861 --> 01:10.401
<b>Rampart
Reflection</b>

01:08.851 --> 01:10.401
Rampart Reflection!

01:25.501 --> 01:28.671
Shield Bash!

01:32.841 --> 01:38.061
He must be using his family name 
to blackmail a guild employee!

01:39.471 --> 01:43.771
How dare he tarnish the Edvaughn 
name after leaving this place?

01:43.771 --> 01:47.401
There's no familial love 
between us anymore, Elymas.

01:47.401 --> 01:50.321
Lord Elymas is an intelligent 
and principled man.

01:50.321 --> 01:54.411
I can't imagine he'd 
strong-arm anyone like that.

01:55.581 --> 01:58.411
We should verify 
the truth first, Lord Aizas.

02:00.961 --> 02:04.421
In that case, Thomas, you go do it.

02:04.691 --> 02:07.501
If he really is using the family name,

02:08.231 --> 02:12.351
have him removed from the guild's roster 
and ban him from re-registering.

02:12.351 --> 02:13.511
And tell him...

02:15.051 --> 02:17.541
If he does anything like this again,

02:17.971 --> 02:20.581
he's a dead man.

02:24.391 --> 02:26.781
It's me, my lord.

02:29.011 --> 02:31.601
Ah, Malice. Come in.

02:37.681 --> 02:40.391
You needn't be so formal, Malice.

02:40.391 --> 02:43.451
You're the future head 
of the family. You're my heir.

02:43.781 --> 02:46.211
You could even call me Father.

02:47.601 --> 02:51.071
Regarding your discussion, 
you're too soft on him.

02:51.731 --> 02:54.641
Thomas favors Elymas too much,

02:54.641 --> 02:57.591
and removing him from 
the guild roster isn't enough.

02:57.851 --> 03:00.281
When Elymas loses his means 
of supporting himself,

03:00.281 --> 03:03.601
he'll become desperate 
and commit more folly.

03:03.941 --> 03:06.201
If he becomes a bandit,

03:06.201 --> 03:09.361
he'll be a massive stain
 on the Edvaughn family name.

03:10.251 --> 03:15.581
You're absolutely right, 
but what are you trying to say, Malice?

03:16.501 --> 03:19.301
You and I should go see what he's up to...

03:21.471 --> 03:24.331
and deal with him directly.

03:35.721 --> 03:36.561
Thanks for waiting.

03:36.561 --> 03:37.571
Hey.

03:38.011 --> 03:42.011
I'm glad you got 
the skillbook you wanted.

04:18.421 --> 04:19.681
<b>Loading</b>

04:30.941 --> 04:32.231
<b>Loading</b>

04:43.571 --> 04:44.871
<b>Loading</b>

04:53.131 --> 04:53.881
<b>Loading</b>

04:55.381 --> 05:00.971
<b>Begin Adventure</b>

04:55.381 --> 05:00.971
<b>Begin Adventure</b>

05:12.061 --> 05:17.021
<b>Episode 11\h\h\h\hInescapable Past</b>

05:13.111 --> 05:16.891
I actually bought 
the Fang of Smoldering Insanity.

05:17.441 --> 05:21.161
It's fine. I said you could.

05:21.161 --> 05:23.451
It's a gift.

05:23.711 --> 05:27.951
You bought me that 
Ironpiercer, didn't you?

05:28.441 --> 05:31.091
That was way less expensive.

05:31.461 --> 05:35.511
Besides, we needed that 
to slay Golden Raana.

05:35.511 --> 05:37.591
I knew I'd make back what I spent.

05:37.991 --> 05:41.471
And you won't with that skill tree?

05:41.471 --> 05:45.221
No, I will. You can be sure of that.

05:45.481 --> 05:47.721
<i>Fang of Smoldering Insanity skillbook.</i>

05:45.761 --> 06:02.241
<b>Fang of Smoldering Insanity Skillbook
 Market Price: 30,000,000G
 Unlocks Fang of Smoldering Insanity skill tree.
Beware of those with this skill tree. Dragging
his shattered body and letting his torn tail flutter,
not even the God of Death dares approach his
unstoppable rampage.</b>

05:47.721 --> 05:50.631
<i>Market price: 30,000,000 gold.</i>

05:50.631 --> 05:54.181
<i>Beware of those with this skill tree.</i>

05:54.181 --> 05:57.801
<i>Dragging his shattered body 
and letting his torn tail flutter,</i>

05:57.801 --> 06:02.241
<i>not even the God of Death dares 
approach his unstoppable rampage.</i>

06:02.551 --> 06:06.281
Um, Ruche, would it be okay 
if I used it now?

06:06.681 --> 06:09.411
I'm worried someone might steal it.

06:10.411 --> 06:12.661
Of course. Please, go right ahead.

06:12.661 --> 06:15.391
But is it actually strong?

06:15.391 --> 06:16.151
What?

06:16.151 --> 06:18.791
Fang of Smoldering Insanity.

06:18.791 --> 06:24.431
The descriptive text makes me 
a little uneasy, but it's safe, right?

06:24.431 --> 06:27.751
It doesn't have any 
weird drawbacks, does it?

06:27.751 --> 06:29.261
It's definitely strong.

06:29.261 --> 06:32.831
With enough skill points, 
it'll really start to shine.

06:34.601 --> 06:39.771
<i>Fang of Smoldering Insanity gives suicidal
combat skills for those prepared to die.</i>

06:40.071 --> 06:47.661
<i>Combining it with the Heavy Knight class 
raises its firepower to absurd levels.</i>

06:50.021 --> 06:53.151
Here goes.

06:54.361 --> 06:55.601
<i>Gulp.</i>

06:54.711 --> 06:55.911
<b>Gulp</b>

06:57.171 --> 06:58.921
<b>Skill Trees: Heavy Knight</b>

06:57.171 --> 06:58.921
<b>Remaining Skill Points: 13</b>

07:01.771 --> 07:06.871
<i>I'll overwrite Defense Booster 
with Fang of Smoldering Insanity.</i>

07:07.431 --> 07:10.431
<b>Skill Trees: Heavy Knight</b>

07:07.431 --> 07:10.431
<b>Remaining Skill Points: 13</b>

07:07.431 --> 07:10.431
<b>Oath of the Heavy Armor</b>

07:07.431 --> 07:09.091
<b>Defense Booster</b>

07:07.431 --> 07:10.431
<b>Beginner Swordsmanship</b>

07:32.201 --> 07:36.711
<b>Oath of the Heavy Armor</b>

07:32.201 --> 07:36.711
<b>Beginner Swordsmanship</b>

07:32.371 --> 07:36.711
<b>Fang of Smoldering Insanity</b>

07:33.571 --> 07:37.301
A-All right! Fang of Smoldering 
Insanity is finally mine!

07:36.711 --> 07:41.041
<b>Skill Trees: Heavy Knight</b>

07:36.711 --> 07:41.041
<b>Remaining Skill Points: 13</b>

07:36.711 --> 07:41.041
<b>Oath of the Heavy Armor


Fang of Smoldering Insanity


Beginner Swordsmanship</b>

07:37.301 --> 07:41.041
Look, Ruche! I got this because of you!

07:42.131 --> 07:47.011
Didn't you say we shouldn't 
show our stats to others?

07:49.211 --> 07:52.431
But I'm starting to feel happy, too.

07:52.701 --> 07:56.131
Are you going to put points into it now?

07:57.011 --> 08:01.611
No. First, I'll put points in Oath 
of the Heavy Armor to grab this skill...

08:10.701 --> 08:15.981
We've gained a lot of levels, so we 
should probably straighten out my gear.

08:16.771 --> 08:21.641
Then why don't we go
 for dungeon drops?

08:21.641 --> 08:22.391
What?

08:23.471 --> 08:28.171
Listen, Ruche, targeting 
specific item drops...

08:28.341 --> 08:34.431
Previous Drops

08:31.131 --> 08:33.001
isn't out of the question.

08:33.001 --> 08:34.431
All right!

08:34.431 --> 08:36.621
You liked my idea!

08:56.491 --> 08:57.861
Who's that?

08:57.861 --> 08:59.681
Idiot, that's the local lord!

08:59.681 --> 09:00.461
What?!

09:00.751 --> 09:02.461
That's the Master Swordsman.

09:02.951 --> 09:05.751
Why, if it isn't Count Edvaughn.

09:06.111 --> 09:10.281
What brings you to our 
humble Adventurer's Guild?

09:10.281 --> 09:13.201
I have something important 
to discuss. Clear the room.

09:13.201 --> 09:15.761
Uh, excuse me?

09:16.161 --> 09:18.771
Why don't we speak in the back?

09:19.641 --> 09:22.771
Did you not hear me? Clear the room.

09:24.351 --> 09:26.641
Th-The guild is closed for the day!

09:26.321 --> 09:31.021
<i>I don't know why he's here, 
but I'd like to avoid Aizas.</i>

09:26.641 --> 09:28.691
Adventurers, please leave 
the building quickly!

09:31.021 --> 09:32.951
<i>He probably feels the same way.</i>

09:33.551 --> 09:36.711
Let's go, Ruche. 
We don't want his attention.

09:36.711 --> 09:38.241
O-Okay.

09:38.521 --> 09:41.611
That's Lord Aizas, isn't it?

09:41.611 --> 09:46.161
I didn't have a good impression of 
the Edvaughn family to begin with,

09:46.161 --> 09:49.181
but he seems overbearing and nasty.

09:52.541 --> 09:55.711
You there, adventurer. You stay.

09:58.541 --> 09:59.781
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

09:59.781 --> 10:03.271
I was just trying to lighten 
the mood by clowning around!

10:03.271 --> 10:04.521
Don't worry, Ruche.

10:08.291 --> 10:09.881
He's not interested in you.

10:10.731 --> 10:15.101
It seems he has business with me.

10:36.341 --> 10:38.051
What say we team up this time?

10:48.471 --> 10:50.691
What does a noble want with me?

10:51.381 --> 10:54.441
How dare you speak to me like that?

10:56.111 --> 10:59.801
Mr. Elymas, you should be more respectful!

10:59.801 --> 11:01.871
Come on, let's apologize!

11:02.641 --> 11:04.151
You.

11:05.401 --> 11:08.121
You're awfully friendly with Elymas.

11:08.121 --> 11:09.441
What are you to him?

11:09.441 --> 11:09.921
Huh?

11:10.381 --> 11:13.981
Y-You know Mr. Elymas?

11:15.491 --> 11:17.941
Ruche, go outside.

11:17.941 --> 11:19.391
This is my problem.

11:19.391 --> 11:20.641
B-But...

11:20.641 --> 11:23.451
If I'm in the way, I'll leave.

11:23.451 --> 11:28.521
But telling me I shouldn't get involved 
just makes me want to stay.

11:28.521 --> 11:32.991
Maybe there's nothing 
I can do by being here.

11:32.991 --> 11:34.031
Ruche.

11:34.031 --> 11:40.031
But friends stand by each other 
in times like these.

11:40.291 --> 11:42.451
Not this time, Ruche.

11:42.451 --> 11:46.411
I can't leave you 
when you look so distraught.

11:46.411 --> 11:50.831
You, a commoner, 
dare to tell us what to do?

11:51.221 --> 11:53.451
Leave at once!

11:53.451 --> 11:54.731
Father.

11:55.171 --> 11:57.501
Let's allow her to stay.

11:58.271 --> 12:00.971
She and Elymas seem quite close.

12:00.971 --> 12:03.851
She could be involved in the rumors.

12:05.171 --> 12:06.461
Fine.

12:07.161 --> 12:12.241
I promised I'd let you 
deal with him anyway.

12:12.241 --> 12:14.271
Count Edvaughn.

12:14.561 --> 12:17.721
Did you hear about this promising man

12:17.721 --> 12:20.531
and come to recruit him 
to your private army?

12:20.531 --> 12:22.721
The news reached you quickly.

12:22.721 --> 12:26.791
This adventurer is courteous and brave.

12:26.791 --> 12:29.961
His name will go down 
in this guild's history.

12:29.961 --> 12:31.521
Guildmaster.

12:32.101 --> 12:34.851
Drop the obvious act.

12:34.851 --> 12:36.881
You already know, don't you?

12:37.161 --> 12:38.091
What?

12:43.471 --> 12:46.971
This man is an Edvaughn!

12:46.971 --> 12:48.431
What?!

12:50.631 --> 12:52.681
Wh-What do you mean?

12:53.061 --> 12:57.441
One of your guild employees 
must be conspiring with this brat.

12:57.441 --> 12:58.281
What?!

12:58.281 --> 13:02.411
Find them all and bring 
them here this instant!

13:02.411 --> 13:05.741
W-Wait. That can't be...

13:08.471 --> 13:10.321
R-Right away, sir!

13:10.321 --> 13:16.031
Mr. Elymas, is Count Aizas...

13:16.031 --> 13:17.391
He's my father.

13:19.531 --> 13:21.301
I hate to say it, but it's true.

13:22.531 --> 13:25.681
You're an embarrassment 
to the Edvaughn family.

13:25.681 --> 13:33.111
I merely exiled you because I believed 
you wouldn't do anything stupid.

13:34.281 --> 13:39.071
Elymas, have you forgotten what I said?

13:39.401 --> 13:41.901
If you used the Edvaughn 
family name again,

13:42.531 --> 13:45.371
I said I'd have your head!

13:56.931 --> 14:00.511
<i>I've been enjoying too much success 
since leaving the count's family.</i>

14:02.581 --> 14:05.511
<i>Aizas came to check on me</i>

14:05.511 --> 14:10.741
<i>because he suspects I cheated my way 
into my unusual promotion.</i>

14:16.041 --> 14:18.441
So that's why you're here.

14:20.271 --> 14:23.451
I haven't been using the family name.

14:23.891 --> 14:25.911
Th-That's right.

14:25.911 --> 14:29.081
Why are you so distrustful of him?

14:36.651 --> 14:38.881
It's impossible. It can't be done.

14:38.881 --> 14:41.171
In just one week,

14:41.651 --> 14:46.541
a single adventurer couldn't 
possibly slay a level 50 Dreamlord.

14:49.761 --> 14:53.151
Father, our goal this time 
is to investigate.

14:53.151 --> 14:55.041
There's no need to rush.

14:55.041 --> 14:55.771
What?

14:56.531 --> 15:01.321
Elymas, I hear you're around level 40.

15:01.321 --> 15:07.321
That's perfect. I just finished using 
Lifeforce Transfer to reach level 45.

15:09.221 --> 15:13.661
We can verify your story 
with a practice fight.

15:13.961 --> 15:15.721
<i>Lifeforce Transfer.</i>

15:15.721 --> 15:18.671
<i>She's been farming EXP 
by killing high-level criminals.</i>

15:19.541 --> 15:21.251
<i>It's barbaric.</i>

15:23.251 --> 15:28.391
If we're around the same level, his combat 
experience should give him the edge.

15:28.391 --> 15:33.221
We need only cross blades briefly 
to determine the truth.

15:35.561 --> 15:37.691
Don't be ridiculous, Malice.

15:38.001 --> 15:40.361
Even if your levels are comparable,

15:40.361 --> 15:43.781
a fight between a Master Swordsman 
and Heavy Knight is a joke.

15:44.921 --> 15:48.161
It's just practice, Father.

15:48.161 --> 15:55.041
And isn't it impressive that he rose 
this far this quickly by himself?

15:55.691 --> 15:59.001
I was just hoping to learn from him.

15:59.311 --> 16:03.001
Of course, if he's lying...

16:03.301 --> 16:07.881
then this practice could also 
be his punishment.

16:09.011 --> 16:11.391
<i>Master Swordsman is a powerful class.</i>

16:11.701 --> 16:14.841
<i>Its Attack and Speed are insanely high,</i>

16:14.841 --> 16:17.721
<i>and many of its skills 
are straightforward and brutal.</i>

16:18.491 --> 16:21.391
<i>Without high Attack or Speed,</i>

16:21.391 --> 16:24.781
<i>the Heavy Knight is stuck defending 
against a Master Swordsman.</i>

16:24.781 --> 16:27.981
<i>Even if I land a hit, 
it won't end the fight.</i>

16:29.131 --> 16:35.911
<i>I can probably put up a bit of a fight, 
but I doubt she'll let it go at that.</i>

16:36.291 --> 16:38.051
This is nonsense.

16:38.051 --> 16:41.711
Why are you so interested 
in Elymas, Malice?

16:41.711 --> 16:43.681
I chose you to be my—

16:43.681 --> 16:46.451
Fine. I accept your mock battle.

16:47.131 --> 16:49.691
But I have one condition.

16:51.161 --> 16:54.261
If you acknowledge my power,

16:54.701 --> 16:57.571
never concern yourself with me again.

16:59.611 --> 17:01.451
You brat!

17:02.101 --> 17:07.381
I'm delighted, Elymas. 
That's what I like to hear.

17:14.521 --> 17:17.241
Mr. Elymas, this is crazy.

17:17.681 --> 17:22.001
It goes without saying, 
but don't kill him, Malice.

17:24.321 --> 17:28.091
<i>This is my chance 
to demonstrate my integrity.</i>

17:28.921 --> 17:32.721
<i>No, with this duel, I'll say 
goodbye to the Edvaughn family.</i>

17:34.141 --> 17:36.761
Nice single-edged sword, Malice.

17:37.811 --> 17:39.411
<i>The Magiblade Watercrow.</i>

17:39.871 --> 17:42.791
<i>It provides a significant boost to Attack.</i>

17:42.791 --> 17:46.271
<i>All she has to do is wildly swing it 
around to be a serious threat.</i>

17:46.731 --> 17:52.781
Father secretly acquired this 
so he could give it to you.

17:54.551 --> 17:56.781
We haven't practiced since we were little.

17:57.081 --> 18:00.941
To be honest, I didn't think 
you hated me this much.

18:08.201 --> 18:09.171
<i>Parry!</i>

18:13.941 --> 18:15.431
Sh-She's so fast!

18:15.971 --> 18:21.081
I'm relieved, Elymas. This will be fun.

18:21.081 --> 18:22.271
After all...

18:24.441 --> 18:29.441
this is the last time I'll play 
with the man I looked up to.

18:29.711 --> 18:34.951
I'll start by cutting off your left arm!

18:46.141 --> 18:48.541
M-Mr. Elymas is being overpowered?

18:50.591 --> 18:53.381
What's wrong? Come on!

18:54.381 --> 18:55.731
Come on!

18:59.181 --> 19:00.681
<b>Elymas Edvaughn</b>

19:03.981 --> 19:07.311
Elymas is being a stubborn fool.

19:07.311 --> 19:10.041
Malice is toying with him.

19:11.771 --> 19:15.821
<b>Elymas Edvaughn</b>

19:12.701 --> 19:15.021
<i>I've already lost about 40% of my HP.</i>

19:15.821 --> 19:19.451
Too slow. That's not quick enough to—

19:21.731 --> 19:22.951
What?!

19:22.951 --> 19:24.221
<i>Vital Slice!</i>

19:23.791 --> 19:25.461
<b>Vital Slice</b>

19:28.171 --> 19:31.791
H-He did it! He landed a direct hit!

19:31.791 --> 19:37.011
<i>A Master Swordsman and Heavy Knight's 
stats are worlds apart!</i>

19:37.901 --> 19:40.851
<i>Did Malice let her guard down?</i>

19:41.341 --> 19:45.781
<i>The Heavy Knight's Attack is low, 
but that should've hurt a bit.</i>

19:45.781 --> 19:49.221
<i>But tricks like that will only work once.</i>

19:49.351 --> 19:54.731
<b>Title: Upsetter
\h\h\hAttack and Speed increase by 15% when 
\h\h\hfighting higher-level enemies.</b>

19:49.751 --> 19:51.801
<i>The Upsetter's Speed boost</i>

19:51.801 --> 19:54.731
<i>and a surprise Shadow Stomp 
barely enabled me to land one hit.</i>

20:06.911 --> 20:08.651
Give me everything you've got, Malice.

20:09.151 --> 20:12.421
It's not like you'll back down 
after that, right?

20:13.651 --> 20:15.421
I'm glad.

20:16.331 --> 20:18.971
You're still you.

20:20.451 --> 20:26.191
I was worried our time together 
would end quickly!

20:30.351 --> 20:35.861
As a token of respect 
for landing a hit on me...

20:40.101 --> 20:44.571
I'll show you a Master Swordsman skill.

20:45.611 --> 20:48.221
Cold-As-Steel Cutter!

20:48.711 --> 20:50.161
She vanished?!

20:50.641 --> 20:54.301
<i>Lightning-fast strikes are what
the Master Swordsman class is all about!</i>

21:15.141 --> 21:17.191
<i>Did I manage to survive?</i>

21:26.201 --> 21:28.241
One more strike.

21:35.421 --> 21:37.201
Mr. Elymas!

21:56.061 --> 21:59.571
<b>Translator:
Sho Stifler

Timer:
Krzysztof Kunc

Editor:
Salem Alabanza

Quality Control:
Gabriella Alabanza

Final Quality Control:
Sriram Gurunathan</b>

23:10.781 --> 23:12.981
<i>My fierce battle against Malice continues.</i>

23:12.981 --> 23:18.061
<i>The Master Swordsman's stat advantage
 and brutal skills are no surprise.</i>

23:18.651 --> 23:22.611
<i>No matter how many cheap tricks a Defense 
specialist like the Heavy Knight uses,</i>

23:22.611 --> 23:23.731
<i>he can't win.</i>

23:24.401 --> 23:26.451
<i>Don't worry, Ruche.</i>

23:26.451 --> 23:30.781
<i>I've got the Fang of Smoldering 
Insanity we acquired together.</i>

23:31.521 --> 23:33.951
<i>Next time, "Malice the Master Swordsman."</i>

23:34.511 --> 23:38.211
<i>It's time to show off 
the Heavy Knight's evolution!</i>
